lugins:[d.Z],className:"prose-base max-w-4xl md:prose-lg prose-a:text-sky-400",children:'\n# Privacy Policy\n\nLast updated: August 31, 2025\n\n## 1. Introduction\n\nWelcome to Upscayl Cloud ("Company", "we", "our", "us"). We provide an online AI image upscaling and enhancement service (the "Service"). This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, how we share it, and your choices. If you do not agree with this policy, please do not use the Service.\n\nWe are committed to privacy by design:\n- We collect only what we need to operate and improve the Service.\n- We do not sell personal information.\n- Your images are not used to train AI models.\n\n## 2. What We Collect\n\nWe collect the following categories of information when you use the Service:\n\n### 2.1 Account Information\n- Email address, display name, and unique user ID from Firebase Authentication\n- Basic profile metadata you choose to provide\n\n### 2.2 Usage and Device Information\n- Event and usage data (e.g., feature usage, performance metrics) collected via PostHog\n- Device type, browser type/version, operating system, approximate location (derived from IP), timestamps\n- Log data from our servers and cloud functions for security, diagnostics, and fraud prevention\n\n### 2.3 Payment and Subscription Information\n- Subscription status, plan details, and transaction metadata from our payment partners (Dodo Payments, and PayPal and/or Lemon Squeezy for existing subscriptions). Stripe may be used for certain workflows. We do not store full card numbers or CVVs; payment data is processed by our payment providers\n\n### 2.4 Uploaded Content and Generated Outputs\n- Images you upload, links you provide for processing, and generated outputs\n- File metadata (e.g., filename, MIME type, size, dimensions) and storage paths\n\n### 2.5 Communications\n- Support correspondence and feedback (email content and headers)\n\n## 3. How We Use Information\n\nWe use your information to:\n- Provide, operate, and maintain the Service\n- Authenticate users, manage accounts, and enforce access controls\n- Process images and deliver outputs\n- Measure performance, improve features, and troubleshoot issues\n- Communicate about updates, billing, and support\n- Detect, prevent, and address fraud, abuse, and security incidents\n- Comply with legal obligations\n\n## 4. Legal Bases (EEA/UK)\n\nWhere applicable law requires a legal basis, we rely on:\n- Performance of a contract (providing the Service)\n- Legitimate interests (security, analytics, service improvement)\n- Consent (where required for optional analytics/cookies)\n- Legal obligations (accounting, compliance)\n\n## 5. Cookies and Similar Technologies\n\nWe use cookies and similar technologies to:\n- Keep you signed in and protect your account (strictly necessary)\n- Measure usage and improve the Service (analytics via PostHog)\n\nYou can control cookies through your browser settings. If your browser sends a Do Not Track (DNT) signal, we will respect it for PostHog where supported. Some features may not function without required cookies.\n\n## 6. Data Retention\n\n- Account records: kept while your account is active and as needed for legal/compliance purposes\n- Usage analytics: retained no longer than necessary for the purposes described above\n- Uploaded input files and URL-retrieved inputs: we aim to retain for up to 1 days from upload, after which they may be deleted or overwritten pursuant to storage lifecycle policies\n- Generated outputs: retained for 180 days, or until you delete them, subject to backup and system logs\n\nNote: Actual deletion timing may vary due to backups, caches, and system safeguards. You can request deletion at any time (see Your Rights).\n\n## 7. How We Share Information\n\nWe do not sell your personal information. We share data only with service providers that help us run the Service, subject to appropriate safeguards:\n\n- Firebase (Google Cloud): authentication, database, serverless functions\n- Amazon Web Services (AWS S3): file storage for uploads/outputs\n- PostHog: product analytics\n- Dodo Payments, PayPal and Lemon Squeezy (and, where applicable, Stripe): payments and subscription management\n- Email (Gmail): transactional communications\n- Infrastructure, security, and monitoring vendors as needed\n\nWe may also share information to comply with the law, protect users and our systems, or during a merger, acquisition, or asset sale.\n\n## 8. International Data Transfers\n\nYour information may be processed and stored in countries different from your own (for example, Google Cloud/Firebase and AWS regions, and our analytics/payment providers). Where required, we implement appropriate safeguards such as contractual clauses and technical measures to protect your data.\n\n## 9. Security\n\nWe employ technical and organizational measures to protect your data, including encryption in transit and at rest provided by our cloud providers, access controls, and monitoring. No system is 100% secure; please use strong passwords, keep credentials confidential, and notify us of any suspected compromise.\n\n## 10. Your Rights\n\nDepending on your location, you may have the right to:\n- Access a copy of your personal information\n- Correct inaccurate information\n- Delete your information (erasure)\n- Restrict or object to processing\n- Data portability\n- Withdraw consent (where processing is based on consent)\n\nTo exercise rights, contact us at support@upscayl.org. We will verify your request and respond as required by law.\n\n## 11. Children’s Privacy\n\nThe Service is intended for users aged 13 and older. If you believe a child under 13 has provided us information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.\n\n## 12. Third-Party Links and Integrations\n\nThe Service may contain links to third-party websites or services. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies. We encourage you to review those policies.\n\n## 13. Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version here and update the “Last updated” date above. Your continued use of the Service after the effective date constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.\n\n## 14. Contact Us\n\nIf you have questions or requests about this policy, please contact:\n\nEmail: support@upscayl.org\n\n---\n\n**Notes:**\n- Images you upload are used only to provide the Service and are not used for AI model training.\n- Payment details are processed by our payment partners; we do not store full card numbers.\n'})]})}),(0,r.jsx)(i.Z,{}),(0,r.jsx)(a.Z,{})]})},68130:function(e,n,t){"use strict";t.d(n,{eW:function(){return r},hn:function(){return o}});let r=195e3,o={PUBLIC_ACCESS:!0,MAX_FILE_SIZE:52428800,MAX_FILES_LENGTH:20,WEBP_MAX_RESOLUTION:16383,JPEG_MAX_RESOLUTION:65535,MAX_TRIAL_INPUT_RESOLUTION:8,MAX_BASIC_INPUT_RESOLUTION:64,MAX_BUSINESS_INPUT_RESOLUTION:64,MAX_TRIAL_OUTPUT_RESOLUTION:16,MAX_BASIC_OUTPUT_RESOLUTION:256,MAX_BUSINESS_OUTPUT_RESOLUTION:512}},89302:function(e,n,t){"use strict";t.d(n,{Q:function(){return r}});let r={NOT_STARTED:"NOT_STARTED",SELECTED_FILE:"SELECTED_FILE",UPLOADING:"UPLOADING",UPLOAD_FAILED:"UPLOAD_FAILED",UPLOADED:"UPLOADED",UPSCALING:"UPSCALING",ENHANCING:"ENHANCING",PROCESSING:"PROCESSING",PROCESSED:"PROCESSED",PROCESS_FAILED:"PROCESS_FAILED"}}},function(e){e.O(0,[9102,3467,1154,5123,2598,419,2230,2888,9774,179],function(){return e(e.s=61540)}),_N_E=e.O()}]);